      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1810, a watering trough built by Hugh Bigham became the town’s central watering point, later known as the running pump.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delmont%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 300 acres granted to William Wilson in 1784 became New Salem when he arrived in 1785, laying the groundwork for the borough.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delmont%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Central Hotel, a historic building, once hosted stagecoach travelers heading to Pittsburgh, reflecting Delmont’s role on early travel routes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delmont%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Delmont’s historic preservation society, founded in the late 1970s, worked to restore local landmarks before eventually disbanding.",
